m  doom eternals greatly increased mobility  and creative level design or where the  game really kicks into a metal guitar  solo and start shredding  especially in its best designed arenas  you're always repositioning taking  opportunities to fill your Larter's with  health and ammo and prioritizing threats  to tune the fight to your liking once  you get the rhythm of eternal it becomes  a brilliant extension of what made doom  2016 so cool and eternal is great at  providing heart-pounding moments when  you barely manage to slice off an  opponent's head just in time to shower  yourself with health and cheap death  then spin around and blast a big foe  with a rocket suddenly tipping the odds  in your favor just about every fight  feels like a speeding train seconds from  going off the rails with disaster only  averted because you're so damn good at  killing stuff there are a ton of fights  in Doom eternal and nearly every one of  them is a heart-pounding  white-knuckle struggle for survival well  the intricacies of combat are the big  focus in doom eternal there's a lot of  other stuff going on too there's an even  bigger focus on platforming and puzzling  out how to traverse levels and find the  myriad secrets and upgrades scattered  within them isn't welcome breather  between fights the platforming is still  a bit iffy at times especially when you  need to make a long jump to grab monkey  bars or sticky walls but falls into the  abyss no longer kill you  making these portions of the game pretty  forgiving there's also a fairly involved  story stretch through doom eternal  although good luck following it if you  don't take the time to read the many  collectible or drops scattered around a  turtle's approach to its storytelling  feels like a fundamental shift from the  satirical jokey approach in 2016 s doom  that game was about an energy company  that got rich off devil worship and a  protagonist who would literally punched  the radio's trying to give him context  f